notes: ATCC173 and TOGO M2399 list 19 g Middlebrook 7H10 agar as a separate input
  from 5 mL glycerol, 100 mL OADC and 900 mL water. This source-qualified identity
  denotes that base input. NCIT:C85509 describes the enriched complete medium, including
  OADC and glycerol, and cannot be asserted as its exact identity. The unqualified
  source label is retained only as non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL. Manufacturer, complete
  base formulation, component IDs and roles are not established and are not invented.
  Exact source-qualified stock/product identity is supported independently of a full
  decomposition. Existing complete-medium owner remains unchanged; cross-shard owner
  reconciliation is required before integration. The unqualified raw source label
  is retained as REJECTED_LABEL solely for provenance because RAW_TEXT also resolves
  globally in the native matcher. The exact source occurrence may bind to this source-qualified
  preparation after coordinator integration; no global same-label binding is proposed.
